# Cloudflare Pages serves every asset with "public, max-age=14400, must-revalidate" by
# default, so the two shared stylesheets (_astro/_city_.*.css is the global chunk, loaded
# on all 2,720 pages) were revalidated on every visit more than four hours apart. Their
# filenames carry a content hash, so a changed file is always a new URL and the old one can
# never go stale: immutable is the correct answer and it removes one blocking round-trip
# from the critical path on repeat and cross-page views.
# Only /_astro/* is hashed. HTML keeps the default must-revalidate so a deploy is picked up
# immediately.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
